<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>The library · Agentic Bible</title><meta name="description" content="The library — Agentic Bible, a sourced reference for AI agents and their technology."><meta property="og:title" content="The library · Agentic Bible"><meta property="og:description" content="The library — Agentic Bible, a sourced reference for AI agents and their technology."><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:site_name" content="Agentic Bible"><meta property="og:url" content="https://agenticbible.si/"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary"><meta name="twitter:title" content="The library · Agentic Bible"><meta name="twitter:description" content="The library — Agentic Bible, a sourced reference for AI agents and their technology."><meta name="robots" content="index, follow"><meta name="color-scheme" content="light"><link rel="canonical" href="https://agenticbible.si/"><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_astro/Base.DyzAbnuc.css"></head><body><a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header shell"><a class="wordmark" href="/"><img src="/favicon.svg" width="36" height="36" alt=""><span>Agentic Bible<span class="wordmark-sub">A living reference</span></span></a><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/" aria-current="page">Library</a><a href="/topics/">Topics</a><a href="/about/">About</a><a href="/history/">History</a></nav><a class="header-search" href="/search/" aria-label="Search the library"><svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="8.5" cy="8.5" r="5.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"></circle><path d="m13 13 4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"></path></svg><span>Search</span><kbd aria-hidden="true">/</kbd></a></header><div class="preview-strip" role="region" aria-label="Edition status"><div class="shell"><span class="status-dot"></span> Preview edition <span class="strip-detail">Sourced working drafts. Editorial review pending.</span></div></div><main id="main" class="shell" tabindex="-1"><section class="library-hero"><div><p class="eyebrow hero-eyebrow">An encyclopedia of agents & their technology</p><h1>A field guide to<br><em>agentic AI.</em></h1><p class="hero-description">Understand the ideas, tools, and protocols behind AI agents. Follow the connections. Go back to the source.</p><a class="text-link" href="#collection">Explore the library <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 2v12m-5-5 5 5 5-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></div><div class="loop-diagram" aria-label="An agent loop: goal, decide, act, observe, then decide again" role="img"><div class="diagram-caption"><span>FIG. 01</span><span>THE AGENT LOOP</span></div><div class="orbit orbit-outer"></div><div class="orbit orbit-inner"></div><div class="diagram-center"><span class="diagram-star"><svg class="asterisk" width="40" height="40" viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 4v32M4 20h32M9 9l22 22M9 31 31 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg></span><span>Goal</span></div><span class="loop-node node-one">01 <b>Decide</b></span><span class="loop-node node-two">02 <b>Act</b></span><span class="loop-node node-three">03 <b>Observe</b></span><span class="diagram-arrow arrow-one"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 3l10 10M3 13h10V3" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span><span class="diagram-arrow arrow-two"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13 3 3 13M3 3v10h10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span><span class="diagram-arrow arrow-three"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 14V2m-5 5 5-5 5 5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span><div class="diagram-note">Action informed by feedback.</div></div></section><div class="library-grid" id="collection"><aside class="topic-sidebar"><p class="eyebrow">Browse by topic</p><nav aria-label="Browse topics"><a class="selected" href="/#collection" aria-current="page">All articles <span>20</span></a><a href="/topics/foundations/">Foundations<span>08</span></a><a href="/topics/capabilities/">Capabilities<span>08</span></a><a href="/topics/protocols/">Protocols<span>04</span></a></nav><div class="sidebar-note"><span class="small-star"><svg class="asterisk" width="40" height="40" viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 4v32M4 20h32M9 9l22 22M9 31 31 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg></span><h3>Knowledge, connected.</h3><p>Every entry points to its evidence and to the ideas around it.</p><a href="/about/">How this library works <svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></a></div></aside><section aria-labelledby="collection-title"><div class="section-heading"><h2 id="collection-title">The starting collection</h2><span>01 — 20</span></div><p class="collection-intro">Core ideas, connected through sources and related entries.</p><ol class="article-list"><li><span class="entry-number">01</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Foundations</span><h3><a href="/articles/ai-agent/">AI agent<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>A system that uses a model to choose actions, observe their results, and work toward a goal within defined limits.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">02</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Capabilities</span><h3><a href="/articles/tool-use/">Tool use<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>The structured handoff between a model’s request and software that can retrieve information or take an action.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">03</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Protocols</span><h3><a href="/articles/model-context-protocol/">Model Context Protocol<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>An open protocol for connecting AI applications to tools, resources, and prompts through a shared interface.</p><span class="entry-meta">4 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">04</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Foundations</span><h3><a href="/articles/agent-orchestration/">Agent orchestration<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>How software coordinates model decisions, tools, state, and delegated work while retaining clear stopping and authority boundaries.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">05</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Capabilities</span><h3><a href="/articles/agent-memory/">Agent memory<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>How an agent stores and retrieves information across steps or sessions, and why persistence, relevance, and truth are separate questions.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">06</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Capabilities</span><h3><a href="/articles/retrieval-augmented-generation/">Retrieval-augmented generation<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>A way to generate responses with retrieved material, with distinct failure points in finding evidence, selecting context, and using it faithfully.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">07</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Foundations</span><h3><a href="/articles/agent-evaluation/">Agent evaluation<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>How to test an agent’s outcomes, interaction history, reliability, and limits without confusing a benchmark score with a deployment guarantee.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">08</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Foundations</span><h3><a href="/articles/prompt-injection/">Prompt injection<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>When untrusted text attempts to redirect an AI system, crossing the boundary between material to process and instructions the system should follow.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">09</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Capabilities</span><h3><a href="/articles/agent-planning/">Agent planning<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>How an agent represents possible steps toward a goal, checks intermediate results, and revises a course of action when assumptions fail.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">10</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Capabilities</span><h3><a href="/articles/durable-agent-execution/">Durable agent execution<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>How an agent workflow records progress and resumes after interruption, while distinguishing replayed results from repeated external actions.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">11</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Protocols</span><h3><a href="/articles/tool-permissions/">Tool permissions<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>The boundaries that determine who may request a tool action, which resource it may affect, and where authorization is enforced.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">12</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Capabilities</span><h3><a href="/articles/agent-sandboxing/">Agent sandboxing<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>How an execution environment restricts code and tools, and why filesystem, network, resource and application boundaries need separate examination.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">13</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Foundations</span><h3><a href="/articles/agent-observability/">Agent observability<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>How traces, metrics and event records help explain an agent run, while keeping operational evidence distinct from factual evaluation and audit authority.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">14</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Foundations</span><h3><a href="/articles/human-oversight/">Human oversight<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>How people can inspect, interrupt, correct and govern agent behavior, with explicit distinctions between action approval, later review and technical enforcement.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">15</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Foundations</span><h3><a href="/articles/context-engineering/">Context engineering<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>How an agent selects and maintains the information available for each model call, with separate boundaries for memory, retrieval and authority.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">16</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Capabilities</span><h3><a href="/articles/structured-outputs/">Structured outputs<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>How schemas constrain the form of model responses while leaving factual correctness, supported features and execution authority as separate checks.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">17</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Protocols</span><h3><a href="/articles/agent-identity/">Agent identity and delegation<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>How software establishes an agent caller’s identity and represents delegated authority without confusing a name or persona with verified permission.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">18</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Protocols</span><h3><a href="/articles/agent-to-agent-communication/">Agent-to-agent communication<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>How agents exchange messages, task state and artifacts across an interface, with separate checks for interoperability, authority and result quality.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">19</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Foundations</span><h3><a href="/articles/agent-budgets/">Agent budgets and termination<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>How an agent bounds turns, requests, time and paid work, and reports incomplete or uncertain outcomes when a limit stops execution.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">20</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Capabilities</span><h3><a href="/articles/computer-use-agents/">Computer-use agents<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>How agents observe and act through browser or desktop interfaces, with separate checks for screen grounding, action effects, isolation and authority.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li></ol><div class="reading-path"><span class="eyebrow">New to the subject?</span><p>Start with the agent. Follow the action. Meet the protocol.</p><a class="text-link" href="/articles/ai-agent/">Begin with AI agent <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 8h12m-5-5 5 5-5 5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></div></section></div></main><footer class="site-footer shell"><div><a class="footer-name" href="/">Agentic Bible</a><p>A little more context. A clearer understanding.</p></div><div class="footer-links"><a href="/about/#editorial">Editorial approach</a><a href="https://github.com/Leshey-Digital/agentic-bible">GitHub <svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></a><span>Preview · October 2026</span></div></footer><script type="module" src="/_astro/Base.astro_astro_type_script_index_0_lang.D-1rZP_q.js"></script></body></html>